From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:26:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 59/86] Outline scrolls to keep the current heading in view

When the heading above the cursor changes and its row is outside the
outline, the outline scrolls just far enough to show it. A row already in
view does not move the outline, and scrolling the outline by hand is not
undone until the current heading changes again. Each tab keeps its own
outline scroll position.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

